        "original_id": "46577735-9431-541e-be83-cb5c4c1ce48a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Awards: Lance Todd Trophy, Harry Sunderland Trophy, Golden Boot\n- Places: AJ Bell Stadium, Salford City Stadium, Barton-upon-Irwell, Eccles, Salford, England\n- Organizations: Salford Red Devils, Leeds, Super League\n- People: Kevin Sinfield\n- Topics: Rugby league, sponsorship naming\n\nFacts:\n- The Lance Todd Trophy is presented at a celebratory dinner at the AJ Bell Stadium, which is the home ground of the Salford Red Devils.\n- The Salford City Stadium is referred to as the AJ Bell Stadium for sponsorship purposes.\n- The AJ Bell Stadium is a rugby stadium in Barton-upon-Irwell, Eccles, Salford, England.\n- Kevin Sinfield played his entire professional career with Leeds.\n- Kevin Sinfield is one of the most successful players in Super League history.\n- Kevin Sinfield captained Leeds to seven Super League championships and two Challenge Cup successes.\n- Kevin Sinfield won the Lance Todd Trophy in 2005.\n- Kevin Sinfield won the Harry Sunderland Trophy in 2009 and 2012.\n- Kevin Sinfield won the Golden Boot in 2012 and is one of only four British-based players to have won it.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
